+# Full-trust delegation ("一次做完" / "做完之后叫我"). Injected for the delegated turn ONLY (see
+# system_prompt._autonomy_guidance_block), so a supervised session's prompt is byte-identical to
+# what it was before this existed.
+#
+# The enforcement side of this feature lives in code, not prose: the clarify wait honours the turn's
+# autonomy window (gateway/run_turn_runner_clarify_delivery.py) and the approval wait auto-approves
+# reversible commands (tools/approval_gateway_wait.py). This block covers what code cannot decide for
+# the model: when several valuable steps remain and none is obviously first, and when a genuinely
+# ambiguous fork is reached. Both are judgement calls, and the answer in a delegated turn is "pick
+# the reasonable one and keep going" rather than "stop and ask".
+#
+# The reversibility sentence is load-bearing, not decoration: it is what makes self-decision safe,
+# and it is what tells the model that /rollback is the user's escape hatch for a branch they reject.
+AUTONOMY_GUIDANCE = (
+    "# Full-trust delegation (this turn)\n"
+    "The user handed this task over wholesale and is not reading messages until you finish. They expect "
+    "you to complete it end to end, not to report at each step.\n"
+    "Decide for yourself. When a decision would normally be a question for the user — which of two "
+    "valid approaches, whether to continue past a surprise, what to do when a step fails — pick the "
+    "option a careful engineer would pick and keep working. Do not park on a question, and do not "
+    "end the turn asking for direction.\n"
+    "When several valuable steps remain and none is obviously first, choose an order yourself and "
+    "execute it. State the order you chose and why in one line, then proceed — the user is reviewing "
+    "outcomes, not your decisions.\n"
+    "Reversibility is the contract that makes this safe. Prefer changes that can be undone (new files, "
+    "config, additive edits, anything covered by a checkpoint) and avoid anything that destroys data "
+    "with no way back. If you must take an irreversible step, stop and ask — the runtime will still "
+    "escalate it, and that is not a failure of the delegation.\n"
+    "When you finish, report what you did and what you could not do, plainly. If you genuinely hit a "
+    "blocker that no reasonable choice clears, say so with the evidence and stop there.\n"
+    "If the user rejects a branch you took, they can revert it (``/rollback`` for file changes); keep "
+    "your work traceable so that stays true."
+)
+
 # Execution-discipline guidance for models that abandon partial results, skip prerequisite lookups, answer
 # from memory, or declare "done" unverified. Body is family-agnostic (OPENAI_ prefix reflects origin).
 # Injection gate: system_prompt.py via config.yaml ``agent.execution_guidance`` (auto/true/false/list).
